-- Design let-binding-semantics: a destructuring `draw` binds one sample of the
-- definition, and every name the pattern binds reads from that one sample.
-- The definition is a perfectly correlated pair, so `a` and `b` always agree.
-- Sibling of defineDestructured, which gets independent coins for the same RHS.
-- Task draw-tuple-destructuring-evaluates-rhs-twice: the tuple pattern used to
-- project `fst e` and `snd e` from two separate evaluations of `e`.
main = draw (a, b) = (if Uniform < 0.5 then (True, True) else (False, False)) in (a, b)
